From 8cbb3ebcce014dbfa8075873bb9265edf52d7ebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:46:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] terrain: simulator side (lifted references, reset
 placement, level curriculum, clip restriction), training loop, warm start

Simulator side (MultiClipMotionCommand, terrain_task):
- one global height map built from the compiled model; the Trainer hands the same object to the world model;
- reference root / anchor raised by the base lift (mean terrain under the robot), each re-anchored reference foot by the
  terrain under it, knees half-way: the same functions (supermimic.terrain.lifts) the analytic reward uses, so mjlab's
  reward functions and the root-height termination work unchanged on the lifted references;
- reset: base lift at the reset pose, raised until no sole point is inside the terrain; exactly 0 on flat tiles;
- level curriculum per finished episode: up = no fall, >= 80 % of the same bins' flat-tile reward and >= 70 % of the
  reference's travel; down = fell before half of the possible steps; flat-tile envs never move;
- non-flat tiles take walk / run / sprint clips only;
- env origins: xy of the tile, z = 0 (state_origin); every replay row stores the origin of its episode.

Training loop: --env.terrain-task, height scan for the actor through ActorScan (same lookup as the imagined rollouts),
--init-from (weights and Adam moments of another run, first layers expanded with zero columns), terrain levels in
the checkpoint, curriculum numbers in the log. Flat-ground runs take none of the new branches.

World model: the root-height input is measured from the base lift (was: the single cell under the root).

Checked on a laptop with tools/terrain/local_env.py (plain MuJoCo, real command term / recorder / mjlab reward
functions): simulator-side lifted reward terms and termination height equal the analytic heads to 1e-5 on the
generated stairs; flat tiles get a lift of exactly 0; a few world-model and policy updates on recorded terrain data run
and the new scan columns start to move. Not yet run under mjlab / MuJoCo-Warp.

